user.description:
SEM has detected the following sensors from your Home Assistant Energy Dashboard:

{summary}

Click **Submit** to continue. Just one more step. EV chargers, heat pumps, tariff, and all other settings are set up later in the new **Configuration** tab on the SEM dashboard — no need to handle them now.

hardware.description:
Last step! SEM auto-detected your inverter's discharge control entity: {discharge_entity}

Leave the dashboard option ON to have SEM build its Lovelace dashboard for you. **Note: this triggers a Home Assistant restart about 5 seconds after install completes.**

Everything else — including your grid peak limit — uses safe defaults that you can tune right after setup: the peak limit from the **Control** tab slider, everything else from the **Configuration** tab on the SEM dashboard — including EV chargers, heat pump, tariff, and battery zones.

pv_naming.description:
Give each solar string a name (e.g. East / South / West). Which slot maps to which panel — the numbering follows your Energy-Dashboard solar list, not compass direction:

{mapping}

Leave a field blank to keep the default (PV1/PV2/…).
